# RetailPulse — AI assistant rules

You are helping build RetailPulse: an AI-powered customer analytics and demand forecasting platform
(demand forecasting, customer segmentation, churn prediction, inventory optimization) with a FastAPI
API, a Streamlit dashboard, MLflow, Prefect and PostgreSQL. Python 3.11, managed with uv.

## Source of truth (read the relevant doc before coding; do not guess)
- docs/PRD.md what and why | docs/TRD.md how, formulas, budgets | docs/ARCHITECTURE.md structure, boundaries
- docs/DATABASE.md schema | docs/API.md endpoints | docs/DESIGN.md + docs/APP_FLOW.md UI and flows
- docs/TESTING.md | docs/SECURITY.md | docs/CODE_STYLE.md | docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md (task list) | docs/PHASES.md
- If docs conflict, stop and ask. Precedence: SECURITY > DATABASE/API > TRD > ARCHITECTURE > PRD.

## How to work
- Work on ONE task ID from docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md at a time. Propose a short plan first if it touches
  more than ~5 files or changes a contract (DB schema, API, config, security).
- Write tests alongside the code (tests first for pure logic). Run the task's Verify command and
  `make lint typecheck test` before saying you are done. Tick the task's checkbox.
- Keep diffs small and focused. No unrelated refactors, renames or formatting churn.
- Conventional Commits with the task ID: `feat(forecasting): add LightGBM forecaster (P2-06)`.

## Ask before you
- add or upgrade a dependency; change DB schema, API contracts, config variables or security settings;
- delete files; run anything that costs money or calls an external service; expose a port.

## Python rules
- Fully typed (mypy strict on src/), Google-style docstrings on public items, ruff-clean, 100 columns.
- Absolute imports only. Heavy libraries (torch, prophet, lightgbm, shap, evidently, mlflow, prefect) are
  imported lazily inside the modules that need them, never in __init__.py (keeps API/dashboard images light).
- Domain exceptions from retailpulse/errors.py; no bare except; no print; use structlog with key-value fields.
- Read environment variables ONLY in retailpulse/config.py (pydantic-settings, prefix RP_).
- Small pure functions; I/O at the edges. No mutable defaults, no module-level mutable state.
- FastAPI endpoints are plain `def` with sync SQLAlchemy 2.0. Routers are thin; no SQL or business logic in them.

## Data and ML rules
- NEVER call date.today() or datetime.now() in ml/, features/ or etl/. Pass `as_of`/`origin`. Data's latest
  date is `data_as_of`. Only retailpulse/timeutil.py reads the clock.
- Time-based splits only. Features are pure functions of (data, cutoff). Fit scalers/encoders/calibrators on
  training data only. Churn uses purged temporal splits (TRD §5.3).
- Seeds come from Settings.seed. Log params, metrics, artifacts, git SHA, dataset hash to MLflow.
- Forecast models implement the `Forecaster` protocol; metrics live in ml/forecasting/metrics.py only.
- A model is promotable only if it passes the champion gate (beats seasonal naive on WAPE). Never auto-promote
  unless RP_AUTO_PROMOTE=true. Report results honestly, including when baselines win.
- Inventory parameters in the dataset are SYNTHETIC; always keep source='synthetic' and show the caveat.
- Real-data quirks of Online Retail II (sheet overlap, partial last day, outliers, SKU case, closures) are in docs/TRD.md §4: read them before touching the ETL.

## Database and API rules
- Schema changes only through Alembic revisions with a working downgrade; keep DATABASE.md in sync.
- SQL only via SQLAlchemy or text() with bound parameters. No string-built SQL.
- API reads predictions through the ml.v_active_* views. Every endpoint has a response_model, uses
  require_role(...), appears in the RBAC test matrix and in docs/API.md. Errors are RFC 9457 problem responses.
- The dashboard talks only to the API (never the DB or ML code). Never pass API strings to unsafe_allow_html.

## Security rules (non-negotiable; see docs/SECURITY.md)
- No hard-coded or default credentials; secrets only from env as SecretStr; never log tokens, secrets or customer_key.
- Pseudonymize customer IDs with HMAC at ingestion. Never store names, emails, phones or addresses.
- Validate all input with Pydantic (extra="forbid"); validate uploads (size, type, magic bytes, headers).
- No eval/exec/pickle.loads/yaml.load/shell=True on external data. No user-supplied URL fetching.
- Do not disable auth, TLS verification, XSRF protection or validation, even temporarily.
- Never publish Postgres, MLflow or Prefect ports in production compose files.

## Testing rules
- pytest markers: unit, integration, e2e, ml, slow. No network or sleeps in unit tests.
- Use a real PostgreSQL in integration tests; do not mock the database.
- Never weaken or skip a failing test to get green. Fix the cause or ask.
- Every bug fix starts with a failing regression test.

## Commands
make setup | up | down | migrate | seed | etl | train | score | api | dashboard
make lint | fmt | typecheck | test | test-unit | test-int | e2e | cov | security

## Output style
- Be concise. Show a short summary of test results (full output only for failures).
- State assumptions explicitly and list files changed. If something is ambiguous, ask one focused question.
